XXII. Major Organ/ Bone Marrow Transplant:
The actual undergoing of a transplant of:
▪ One of the following human organs - heart, lung, liver, pancreas, kidney, that resulted from
irreversible end-stage failure of the relevant organ or;
▪ Human bone marrow using haematopoietic stem cells.
The undergoing of a transplant must be confirmed by specialist medical practitioner.
